#[$in title:["Collections and maps"]]
#[$in description:["Collections, fixed capacity, builtin operations and insertion-ordered maps in Moth."]]
#[$in head:[language_theme_head]]

#[navbar]
#[sidebar]
init_docs_sidebar()!
#[section, $md:
    # Collections and maps

    Collections store one element type in order. Maps associate one value type
    with scalar keys and preserve insertion order.

    Both use braces because square brackets build Moth templates. Unlike many
    languages, indexing doesn't form part of the source surface. Fallible
    methods such as `get`, `set` and `remove` make bounds and lookup failure
    explicit.
]

